From f4a19f5644aa77b5fdab4c243ffffee93234ad60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oskari Rauta <oskari.rauta@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 12:55:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 101/111] clk: ingenic: add the T41 clock driver

clk-t41.c and its dt-bindings header come from the Ingenic 4.4.94 BSP.
The shared parts of the Ingenic clock layer diverged between the t40 and
t41 BSP drops, so clk-t40.c and clk-t41.c cannot both build against one
version of clk.h and clk-pll.h. Upstream resolved this by rewriting the
shared files in T41's favour, which changes T40. Here each divergence is
put behind CONFIG_SOC_T41, which is safe because SOC_T40, SOC_T41 and
SOC_X2000_V12 are arms of a single Kconfig choice.

clk-pll.h: T41's rate table carries an extra charge-pump resistor field
"rg" and its PLL_DESC needs the matching register field position, so
PLL_RATE gained an argument and PLL_DESC went from 12 to 14. Both macros
and the two structs keep their old form for every other SoC.

clk-pll.c: T41 encodes the dividers as N-1 with od0 as a power of two,
giving rate = ((prate/1e6) * (m+1) * 2) / ((n+1) * 2^od0 * (od1+1)), and
it must write the rg field when setting a rate. T40's plain form is
preserved unchanged under #else.

clk.c/clk.h: T41 cannot restore a clock divider register by writing the
saved word back - each CDR has a change-enable bit that must be set for
the write to take. It therefore describes the registers it preserves
across suspend with REG_SLEEP() descriptors instead of bare offsets.
The old ingenic_clk_reg_dump API has no users outside clk.c and is not
used by clk-t40.c at all, so the new API is added ALONGSIDE it rather
than replacing it, and clk.o comes out byte-identical for T40.
---
